      "title": "Overview",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.7",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# \ud83c\udfac\u2728 Video Watermark Removal\n\nRemove annoying watermarks from your video automatically, frame by frame. Especially useful for Sora-style watermarks. It's not perfect and can leave behind some artifacts, but it's fast and gets the job done.\n\n## \ud83e\udde0 How it works\n\n1. \ud83c\udfa5 **Load Video**  \n   Splits your video into frames and keeps the original audio.\n\n2. \ud83d\udd0d **Detect Watermark (SAM3)**  \n   Uses `SAM3Segment` with the prompt **\"watermark\"** to find the watermark in each frame and generate a mask.\n\n3. \ud83e\udee7 **Refine Mask**  \n   The mask is grown and feathered so coverage is solid and edges blend smoothly.\n\n4. \ud83e\uddfc **Remove Watermark**  \n   The refined mask is passed into `LaMa Inpaint (AusBoss)` using `big-lama.pt`.\n\n5. \ud83c\udf9e\ufe0f **Rebuild Video**  \n   Frames are stitched back together with the original audio and FPS preserved.\n\n## \ud83d\udce6 Model setup\n\nPlace `big-lama.pt` at `ComfyUI/models/lama/big-lama.pt`, then restart ComfyUI. The AusBoss node never downloads models automatically.\n\n## \ud83d\udca1 Notes\n\n- \u2705 Works best with consistent/static watermarks\n- \u2705 Especially useful for Sora watermarks\n- \ud83e\udeb6 Feathering helps avoid ugly edges\n- \ud83d\udce6 Outputs a clean H264 MP4\n\n## \ud83d\udce6 Requires\n\n- \ud83e\udde9 **ComfyUI-AusBoss** \u2014 LaMa Inpaint + Select Frame\n- \ud83e\udde9 **ComfyUI-RMBG** \u2014 SAM3 segmentation\n- \ud83e\udde9 **rgthree-comfy** \u2014 comparer, labels, group toggles\n- \ud83d\udce5 **Model**: place a TorchScript `big-lama.pt` in `ComfyUI/models/lama/`"
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    }
  ],
